      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 honda civic is making this really loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be the serpentine belt? can you explain how that belt actually works and why it would make that kind of noise if it's worn out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a multi-purpose belt that drives several accessories in your engine, such as the alternator, power steering pump, and air conditioning compressor. If it is worn out, it may slip, causing unusual noises when accelerating because the belt can no longer maintain proper tension and power transfer to these accessories. Moreover, an old or damaged belt might also contact other components, creating friction and generating noise. It's best to inspect this belt by looking at its tension and wear and replacing it if necessary to resolve the squealing noise.",
